# Frontend design schema

Canonical tokens live in `apps/web/src/index.css` under `:root`. Treat that file as the **single source of truth** for surfaces, typography, radius, and default shadows.

## Direction

**Signal Floor** — cool mist desk atmosphere, deep navy ink, teal pulse accent. Display type is Syne; UI/body is DM Sans.

## Tokens (reference)

| Token | Role |
|-------|------|
| `--bg`, `--bg-deep`, `--fg`, `--fg-muted` | Page atmosphere, primary text, secondary text |
| `--accent`, `--accent-hover`, `--accent-soft` | Primary actions, focus ring, soft fills |
| `--card`, `--card-solid`, `--card-border`, `--shadow` | Elevated surfaces and separation |
| `--radius`, `--radius-sm` | Default and smaller corner radius |
| `--up`, `--up-soft`, `--down`, `--down-soft` | Market direction hues |
| `--font`, `--font-display` | Body (DM Sans) and brand/display (Syne) |
| `--chart-stroke` | Price series stroke color |

## Rules

1. **Prefer CSS variables** for layout chrome: backgrounds, borders, foreground, accents. Avoid new hard-coded hex/rgb except where a semantic token already covers the meaning.
2. **Add new primitives in `:root` first**, then wire components with `var(--…)`—do not scatter one-off palette values across TSX or CSS without a matching token when the color is reused.
3. **Focus**: use `:focus-visible` patterns consistent with globals (accent outline)—do not remove focus outlines without an accessible replacement.
4. **Consistency**: spacing and component layout follow patterns in `app.css`; match established gaps unless changing the shell intentionally.

### Example

```css
/* Good */
.panel {
  background: var(--card);
  border: 1px solid var(--card-border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  color: var(--fg);
}

/* Avoid when a semantic token fits */
.panel {
  background: #ffffff;
  color: #2b302b;
}
```

When introducing dark mode later, extend the schema with a class or `prefers-color-scheme` block on the same token names rather than branching colors inside every component.
